ue true or false. This makes the applicability test incompatible with the canonical relationship and prevents valid detached-strut structure nodes from satisfying the intended condition.","required_change":"Model detached-strut use by the presence of nltl:hasDetachedStrut values, remove sh:datatype xsd:boolean and sh:hasValue true/false, and retain the detached-strut node/evidence constraints on those object values.","regression_guard":"Preserve nltl:hasDetachedStrut as an object relationship to nltl:detachedStrutStructure, not as a boolean datatype property.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"},{"category":"LOGIC","location":"gen:TRF064ShipShape / first sh:or branch","problem":"The no-detached-strut alternative requires one nltl:hasDetachedStrut value equal to false via sh:minCount 1 and sh:hasValue false. That encodes a false literal rather than absence of the object relationship, so a ship with no detached strut cannot satisfy the normal plated-bossing alternative.","required_change":"Encode the no-detached-strut condition as absence of nltl:hasDetachedStrut, for example with sh:not around a property shape requiring at least one value, while retaining the plated-bossing requirements.","regression_guard":"Ensure the normal alternative is satisfied when nltl:hasDetachedStrut is absent and does not require an invented boolean value.","blocking":true,"needs_vocabulary_resolution":false,"source":"SEMANTIC"}],"generator_elapsed_ms":31971.656,"validator_elapsed_ms":23698.298}
